@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1741 = private unnamed_addr constant [602 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unused variables in loops (e.g., `for` and `while` statements).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADefining a variable in a loop statement that is never used can confuse\0Areaders.\0A\0AIf the variable is intended to be unused (e.g., to facilitate\0Adestructuring of a tuple or other object), prefix it with an underscore\0Ato indicate the intent. Otherwise, remove the variable entirely.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afor i, j in foo:\0A    bar(i)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afor i, _j in foo:\0A    bar(i)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 8: Naming Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#naming-conventions)\0A", align 1
