@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1771 = private unnamed_addr constant [525 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `set()` calls that take unnecessary list or tuple literals\0Aas arguments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIt's unnecessary to use a list or tuple literal within a call to `set()`.\0AInstead, the expression can be rewritten as a set literal.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aset([1, 2])\0Aset((1, 2))\0Aset([])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A{1, 2}\0A{1, 2}\0Aset()\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as unsafe, as it may occasionally drop comments\0Awhen rewriting the call. In most cases, though, comments will be preserved.\0A", align 1
