@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1783 = private unnamed_addr constant [604 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for \22TODO\22 comments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A\22TODO\22 comments are used to describe an issue that should be resolved\0A(usually, a missing feature, optimization, or refactoring opportunity).\0A\0AConsider resolving the issue before deploying the code.\0A\0ANote that if you use \22TODO\22 comments as a form of documentation (e.g.,\0Ato [provide context for future work](https://gist.github.com/dmnd/ed5d8ef8de2e4cfea174bd5dafcda382)),\0Athis rule may not be appropriate for your project.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef greet(name):\0A    return f\22Hello, {name}!\22  # TODO: Add support for custom greetings.\0A```\0A", align 1
