@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1816 = private unnamed_addr constant [917 x i8] c"## What it does\0ACheck for unrecognized `sys.platform` checks. Platform checks should be\0Asimple string comparisons.\0A\0A**Note**: this rule is only enabled in `.pyi` stub files.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASome `sys.platform` checks are too complex for type checkers to\0Aunderstand, and thus result in incorrect inferences by these tools.\0A`sys.platform` checks should be simple string comparisons, like\0A`if sys.platform == \22linux\22`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aif sys.platform.startswith(\22linux\22):\0A    # Linux specific definitions\0A    ...\0Aelse:\0A    # Posix specific definitions\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AInstead, use a simple string comparison, such as `==` or `!=`:\0A```pyi\0Aif sys.platform == \22linux\22:\0A    # Linux specific definitions\0A    ...\0Aelse:\0A    # Posix specific definitions\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation: Version and Platform checking](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/directives.html#version-and-platform-checks)\0A", align 1
