@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1883 = private unnamed_addr constant [953 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for imports that are required at runtime but are only defined in\0Atype-checking blocks.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe type-checking block is not executed at runtime, so if the only definition\0Aof a symbol is in a type-checking block, it will not be available at runtime.\0A\0AIf [`lint.flake8-type-checking.quote-annotations`] is set to `true`,\0Aannotations will be wrapped in quotes if doing so would enable the\0Acorresponding import to remain in the type-checking block.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING\0A\0Aif TYPE_CHECKING:\0A    import foo\0A\0A\0Adef bar() -> None:\0A    foo.bar()  # raises NameError: name 'foo' is not defined\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport foo\0A\0A\0Adef bar() -> None:\0A    foo.bar()\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-type-checking.quote-annotations`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 563: Runtime annotation resolution and `TYPE_CHECKING`](https://peps.python.org/pep-0563/#runtime-annotation-resolution-and-type-checking)\0A", align 1
