@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2075 = private unnamed_addr constant [447 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `typing.Text`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`typing.Text` is an alias for `str`, and only exists for Python 2\0Acompatibility. As of Python 3.11, `typing.Text` is deprecated. Use `str`\0Ainstead.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom typing import Text\0A\0Afoo: Text = \22bar\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afoo: str = \22bar\22\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.Text`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Text)\0A", align 1
